{
  "about": "Which game events play which sound id. For each event the first rule whose conditions all hold plays; no rule, no sound. Conditions: `warhead` or `weapon` (the generic id fired or bursting), `building` (true or false: what was destroyed or placed), `armour` (the armour class of what was destroyed), `local` (true: only for the player at this screen), `power` (`short`: the player just ran short of power; `restored`: they just stopped being short) and `factory` (the generic id of the factory a unit came out of). A rule with `also` plays as well as the next rule that holds rather than instead of it. `silent` lists the events that play nothing on purpose, so a new event can't be forgotten: every event is in a rule or in `silent`, and a test checks it. `loops` are not events: each says which loop plays while a unit the local player can see is `moving` (on the ground), `flying`, `mining` or `unloading` (harvesters), optionally only for one `armour`; the first that holds for a unit is its loop.",
